### Terraform Version 0.15.0

### Terraform Configuration Files

```terraform

variable "firstterraform"   {
  type    = bool
  default = false
}

locals {
  assume_roles = var.firstterraform ? [] : [ { 
    role_arn  = "arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/security-admin"
  } ]
}

provider "aws" {
  alias  = "security-admin-eu-west-1"
  dynamic "setting" {                # We dont assume-role the first time
    for_each = local.assume_roles
    content {
      assume_role {
        role_arn     = setting.value["role_arn"]
        session_name = "terraform"
      }
    }
  }
  region = "eu-west-1"
}
```

### Expected Behavior

I expected the assume_role {} block to be included if var.firstterraform was set to true

### Actual Behavior

```
Error: Unsupported block type
│ 
│   on provider.tf line 14, in provider "aws":
│   14:       assume_role {
│ 
│ Blocks of type "assume_role" are not expected here.
```

### Steps to Reproduce

The above terraform snippet

### Additional Context

I am trying to create a provider that works for a brand new aws account when all you have is an access key/secret key - but after the first terraform, which creates an aws role, the provider uses the assume_role instead

